utput":"1991-12-26","later-events_catalog":"1991-12-26","stage19_causal_queue":"1991-12-26"},"source_ladder_exhausted_proposed":[],"status":"MACHINE DRAFT - UNVERIFIED; not a claim; see jobs/claim-drafts/AGENT_GUIDE.md"},"claim":{"instrument_id":"EO:12786","later_source_search":[],"operative_clauses":[{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Section 1. Statutory pay systems.  The rates of basic pay or salaries of the  \nfollowing statutory pay systems are set forth on the schedules attached hereto  \nand made a part hereof:","original_source":{"page_or_item":"56 FR 67453, PDF pages 323-333; Sec. 1 (lead-in)","sha256":"7e116b59e55ff211cc6997bb758db37958459b155bc572c3b1000f3453fac4d1","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1991-12-30/pdf/FR-1991-12-30.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12786#sec1","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) The General Schedule (5 U.S.C. 5303, 5332(a)) at Schedule 1;","original_source":{"page_or_item":"56 FR 67453, PDF pages 323-333; Sec. 1(a)","sha256":"7e116b59e55ff211cc6997bb758db37958459b155bc572c3b1000f3453fac4d1","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1991-12-30/pdf/FR-1991-12-30.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12786#sec1(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) The Foreign Service Schedule (5 U.S.C. 5303; 22 U.S.C. 3963) at Schedule  \n2; and","original_source":{"page_or_item":"56 FR 67453, PDF pages 323-333; Sec. 1(b)","sha256":"7e116b59e55ff211cc6997bb758db37958459b155bc572c3b1000f3453fac4d1","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1991-12-30/pdf/FR-1991-12-30.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12786#sec1(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(c) The schedules for the Veterans Health Administration of the Department  \nof Veterans Affairs (5 U.S.C. 5303; 38 U.S.C. 7404; section 301(a) of Public Law\n102- 40) at Schedule 3.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"56 FR 67453, PDF pages 323-333; Sec. 1(c)","sha256":"7e116b59e55ff211cc6997bb758db37958459b155bc572c3b1000f3453fac4d1","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1991-12-30/pdf/FR-1991-12-30.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12786#sec1(c)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 2. Senior Executive Service.  Pursuant to section 5382 of title 5, United  \nStates Code, the rates of basic pay for members of the Senior Executive  \nService are set forth on Schedule 4 attached hereto and made a part hereof.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"56 FR 67453, PDF pages 323-333; Sec. 2","sha256":"7e116b59e55ff211cc6997bb758db37958459b155bc572c3b1000f3453fac4d1","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1991-12-30/pdf/FR-1991-12-30.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12786#sec2","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 3. Executive salaries.  The rates of pay or salaries for the following offices  \nand positions are set forth on the schedules attached hereto and made a part  \nhereof:","original_source":{"page_or_item":"56 FR 67453, PDF pages 323-333; Sec. 3 (lead-in)","sha256":"7e116b59e55ff211cc6997bb758db37958459b155bc572c3b1000f3453fac4d1","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1991-12-30/pdf/FR-1991-12-30.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12786#sec3","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) The Executive Schedule (5 U.S.C. 5312-5316, 5318) at Schedule 5;","original_source":{"page_or_item":"56 FR 67453, PDF pages 323-333; Sec. 3(a)","sha256":"7e116b59e55ff211cc6997bb758db37958459b155bc572c3b1000f3453fac4d1","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1991-12-30/pdf/FR-1991-12-30.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12786#sec3(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) The Vice President (3 U.S.C. 104) and the Congress (2 U.S.C. 31) at  \nSchedule 6; and","original_source":{"page_or_item":"56 FR 67453, PDF pages 323-333; Sec. 3(b)","sha256":"7e116b59e55ff211cc6997bb758db37958459b155bc572c3b1000f3453fac4d1","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1991-12-30/pdf/FR-1991-12-30.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12786#sec3(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(c) Justices and judges (28 U.S.C. 5 ,44(d), 135, 252, and 461(a)) at Schedule 7.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"56 FR 67453, PDF pages 323-333; Sec. 3(c)","sha256":"7e116b59e55ff211cc6997bb758db37958459b155bc572c3b1000f3453fac4d1","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1991-12-30/pdf/FR-1991-12-30.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12786#sec3(c)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 4. Uniformed services. Pursuant to section 601 of Public Law 102-190, the  \nrates of monthly basic pay (37 U.S.C. 203(a)), the rates of basic allowances for  \nsubsistence (37 U.S.C. 402), and the rates of basic allowances for quarters (37  \nU.S.C. 403(a)) for members of the uniformed services are set forth at Schedule  \n8 attached hereto and made a part hereof.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"56 FR 67453, PDF pages 323-333; Sec. 4","sha256":"7e116b59e55ff211cc6997bb758db37958459b155bc572c3b1000f3453fac4d1","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1991-12-30/pdf/FR-1991-12-30.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12786#sec4","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) Pursuant to section 302 of the  \nFederal Employees Pay Comparability Act of 1990, as incorporated in section  \n529 of Public Law 101-509, employees under the statutory pay systems cov­\nered under section 1 of this order, and members of the United States Park  \nPolice, who are assigned to a duty station located in one of the geographical  \nareas listed in Schedule 9 shall be entitled, except as may be provided under  \nsubsection (b) of this section, to receive an interim geographic adjustment at  \nthe rate shown on Schedule 9, which schedule is attached hereto and made a  \npart hereof.\n\n=== PDF page 324 of 344 ===\n67454 Federal Register / Vol. 56, No. 250 / Monday. December 30,1991 / Presidential Documents\n(b) (1) The Office of Personnel Management shall prescribe regulations  \ngoverning the application of interim geographic adjustments to General Sched­\nule employees, including the determination of what, if any, geographic adjust­\nment shall be payable in the case of employees receiving special pay rates.\n(2) The Secretary of State shall prescribe regulations governing the applica­\ntion of interim geographic adjustments to employees under the Foreign Service  \nSchedule, consistent with the regulations and determinations prescribed under  \nparagraph (1) of this subsection.\n(3) The Secretary of Veterans Affairs shall prescribe regulations governing  \nthe application of interim geographic adjustments to employees under the  \nschedules for the Veterans Health Administration of the Department of Veter­\nans Affairs, consistent with the regulations and determinations prescribed  \nunder paragraph (1) of this subsection.\n(4) The Secretary of the Interior shall prescribe regulations governing the  \napplication of interim geographic adjustments to members of the United States  \nPark Police, consistent with the regulations and determinations prescribed  \nunder paragraph (1) of this subsection.\n(c) The Office of Personnel Management is hereby designated and empow­\nered to exercise the authority of the President under section 302(c)(1)(D) of the  \nFederal Employees Pay Comparability Act of 1990, as incorporated in section  \n529 of Public Law 101-509, to extend the application of interim geographic  \nadjustments shown on Schedule 9, upon the request of an agency head, to  \nemployees who would not otherwise be covered.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"56 FR 67453, PDF pages 323-333; Sec. 5(a)","sha256":"7e116b59e55ff211cc6997bb758db37958459b155bc572c3b1000f3453fac4d1","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1991-12-30/pdf/FR-1991-12-30.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12786#sec5(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 6. Effective dates.  The rates of monthly basic pay and allowances for  \nsubsistence and quarters for members of the uniformed services provided for  \nat Schedule 8 are effective on January 1, 1992. The other schedules provided  \nfor herein are effective on the first day of the first applicable pay period  \nbeginning on or after January 1,1992.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"56 FR 67453, PDF pages 323-333; Sec. 6","sha256":"7e116b59e55ff211cc6997bb758db37958459b155bc572c3b1000f3453fac4d1","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1991-12-30/pdf/FR-1991-12-30.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12786#sec6","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 7. Executive Order No. 12736 of December 12, 1990, is superseded.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"56 FR 67453, PDF pages 323-333; Sec. 7","sha256":"7e116b59e55ff211cc6997bb758db37958459b155bc572c3b1000f3453fac4d1","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1991-12-30/pdf/FR-1991-12-30.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12786#sec7","state_at_cutoff":null}],"original_representation":{"page_or_item":"56 FR 67453, PDF pages 323-333","sha256":"7e116b59e55ff211cc6997bb758db37958459b155bc572c3b1000f3453fac4d1","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1991-12-30/pdf/FR-1991-12-30.pdf"},"research_rationale":"","savings_residuals":null,"schema":"eo-lifecycle-claim/v1","unresolved_material_gaps":["DRAFT: state_at_cutoff not decided for 13 clause(s); clause inventory completeness not confirmed","DRAFT: whole-order ending not established","DRAFT: savings and residual effects not closed","DRAFT: later_source_search not recorded (machine searches are proposals only; paste them after judging them adequate and resolving every CONFLICT line)"],"whole_order_end":null,"whole_order_status":"no"},"draft_schema":"eo-claim-draft/v1","instrument_id":"EO:12786"}
